/target
# The local release bundle: installers and archives built on this machine, not
# source. The anchor keeps `crates/ui/dist` — the window's frontend, which is
# source — visible; ignoring the folder does not stop a build writing into it.
/dist/
# The bytecode a fixture generator leaves beside itself when it runs, not source:
# `test-data/make_*.py` writes it into `test-data/__pycache__`, and a script run
# through `py_compile`, imported with its cache turned off, or compiled beside
# itself leaves a `*.pyc` next to the source instead. Neither is ever committed.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# What a conversion writes beside the document it read: `pdfextractor-cli -i
# doc.docx` with no `-o` writes `doc.json` and a `doc_images/` directory next to
# the document, so a hand-run over `test-data/` leaves JSON and images beside a
# fixture — the litter that left `test-data/real/mathtype_images/` in the corpus.
# The goldens' own image directories are fixtures their pages name, so those are
# kept.
#
# The JSON rule names the two folders that litter can land in rather than every
# `*.json` in the repository. A repository-wide `*.json` also swallowed source —
# the window's capabilities, the golden references, Docling's schema — so each one
# needed an exception, and the list grew with every source file; a file added
# without its exception (`crates/ui/capabilities/default.json`) was silently absent
# from a fresh checkout. Source JSON is tracked by default now, and only a
# conversion's own output is ignored.
/test-data/*.json
/test-data/real/*.json
*_images/
!test-data/golden/**/*_images/
# What `tauri-build` writes out of the window's capabilities: schema and ACL
# manifests, rebuilt by the build script whenever they change, never edited by
# hand. Ignored as the directory it is, not by extension.
/crates/ui/gen/
